# ==============================================================================
# sound-hdmi.config – display audio and APU audio: off
# ==============================================================================
# Everything in this fragment is audio that rides on graphics hardware, for both
# GPUs in this machine:
#   dGPU RX 9070:  HDMI/DP audio through its own HDA codec (0000:03:00.1)
#   Raphael iGPU:  HDMI/DP audio through the Ryzen HD Audio controller
#                  (0000:17:00.6, [1022:15e3]) plus the AMD ACP audio block
#
# Sound over the monitor is not wanted here — every audio device on this system
# is USB (see sound-usb.config) — so all of it is off.
#
# This is also the whole kernel-config surface of the iGPU. Raphael carries a
# small RDNA2 iGPU, currently disabled in the BIOS and not on the PCI bus, but
# it needs no Kconfig symbol of its own: amdgpu handles IP_VERSION(10, 3, 6)
# unconditionally and only DRM_AMDGPU_SI/CIK are ASIC-gated, both long disabled.
# Enabling the iGPU in the BIOS therefore changes nothing here — only driving a
# display from it and wanting sound on that display does.
#
# To re-enable display audio, replace the negatives below with:
#   CONFIG_SND_HDA_INTEL=m
#   CONFIG_SND_HDA_GENERIC=m
#   CONFIG_SND_HDA_CODEC_HDMI=m
#   CONFIG_SND_HDA_CODEC_HDMI_ATI=m
# and drop the SND_SOC line. Check the generated .diff afterwards.
# ==============================================================================

# --- ASoC --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Load-bearing for the HDA removal, not merely tidy-up: SND_SOC_INTEL_AVS selects
# SND_SOC_HDA, which selects the hidden SND_HDA core and rebuilds the entire HDA
# stack even with every controller below disabled. Also drops the AMD ACP APU
# audio drivers, which belong to the same graphics-adjacent audio path.
# CONFIG_SND_SOC is not set

# --- HDA controllers: the two entry points, neither under ASoC ---------------
# CONFIG_SND_HDA_INTEL is not set
# CONFIG_SND_HDA_ACPI is not set

# --- HDMI/DP codecs ----------------------------------------------------------
# Redundant while SND_HDA is gone — these live inside "if SND_HDA" in
# sound/hda/codecs/Kconfig. Kept so the intent is greppable by name, and so
# display audio stays off if a controller above is ever restored.
# CONFIG_SND_HDA_CODEC_HDMI is not set
# CONFIG_SND_HDA_CODEC_HDMI_ATI is not set
# CONFIG_SND_HDA_CODEC_HDMI_GENERIC is not set
